1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,000
Built your team with only favorites? Careful: that can cost you Judocoins.

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:12,000
Team's ready… now what? Here, you play two scoreboards.

3
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:20,000
Points move you up the ranking. Judocoins decide the team you can afford next round.

4
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:29,000
Every athlete's price is a points target. Score more than he costs? He rises. Score less? He drops.

5
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:40,000
Look at this favorite: he cost eighteen. Won one fight by ippon, lost the next by waza-ari: eight points. He dropped to thirteen… and you lost five Judocoins.

6
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:48,000
Now a bargain at six who scored sixteen. He rose to eleven, and you gained two and a half.

7
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:56,000
See it? When an athlete rises, you keep half. When he drops, you take the whole drop.

8
00:00:56,000 --> 00:01:05,000
Favorites rise too, if they score more than they cost: an eighteen who scores twenty-four goes to twenty-one.

9
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:10,000
And your captain doubles the points… not the Judocoins.

10
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:20,000
So don't just ask who'll win. Ask who'll score more than he costs. Build your team on Ippon League.
